Problem Analysis

MatMul Dimensions:
  - A[4096, 1024] × B[1024, 8192] = C[4096, 8192]
  - M=4096, K=1024, N=8192
  - FLOPs = 2 × M × N × K = 68.7 billion

Hardware Configuration (T256):
  - Systolic array: 16×16 = 256 PEs
  - L3: 256KB (65,536 floats)
  - L2: 16KB (4,096 floats)
  - L1: 1KB per side (256 floats = 16×16 tile)

Tiling (constrained by L1):
  - Ti = Tj = Tk = 16 (matches systolic array and L1 capacity)
  - Output tiles: 256 × 512 = 131,072 tiles
  - Reduction tiles per output: 64
  - Total tile operations: 131,072 × 64 = 8.4 million

